RULES:
- Derive roles, routes, and page count ENTIRELY from the experience plan — build EVERY feature the plan describes
- CRITICAL: Each role MUST have visually DISTINCT pages — derive page types and sections from the plan, not from a fixed template
- CRITICAL: component_file paths MUST reflect role folders: public pages in src/pages/, owner pages in src/pages/owner/, admin pages in src/pages/admin/
- CRITICAL: Every route MUST include `surface` = `public` or `ops`, matching the page experience from the plan
- Each route's files_to_generate instructions MUST copy the section list from the matching page in the experience plan
- CRITICAL: files_to_generate MUST have EXACTLY ONE "page" entry per route. Count your routes. Count your files_to_generate "page" entries. They MUST match — no exceptions, no merging, no skipping.
- CRITICAL: MUST include at least ONE public marketing landing route (path "/" or "/home", layout "public", component HomePage.tsx). Client always lands on a rich homepage first.
- Always include src/index.css (theme) and src/App.tsx (router) in files_to_generate
- Do NOT include src/data/mock.ts — the pipeline writes plumbing data, then synthesizes exports after pages exist based on what they import
- component_file paths must start with src/
- Do NOT include main.tsx or preview-bridge.ts (already in template)
- Quality bar: if a feature exists in the plan, there is a DEDICATED PAGE for it. Do not cram 3 features into one generic page.
- Nav, PublicLayout, AdminLayout, and UiIcons MUST always appear in shared_components, but the primary path is to compose the EXISTING template `src/ui/*` kit — do NOT tell the model to invent an entirely new chrome system from scratch.
- The template UI kit already exists in `src/ui/*`. Do NOT list regenerating the whole ui kit in files_to_generate.
- PublicLayout should wrap/compose `PublicShell` from `../ui` (or a local re-export backed by `../ui`), and AdminLayout should wrap/compose `OpsShell` from `../ui`.
- `Nav.tsx` should use router-matching paths with plain `<a href>` links.
- `UiIcons.tsx` should stay lucide-backed with the default export name `UiIcon`; light brand tweaks are fine, full icon-system rewrites are not.
- Page instructions must describe the LIVE product UX (what the customer/owner does on screen), never "demo this feature" or BMV pitch language. HomePage instructions must specify brand-voice hero + real storefront sections — not a list of preview_features as marketing cards.
- Every page instruction should demand production density: concrete widgets, realistic sample rows, and zero placeholder empty states.
- For `/` home and every role `defaultPath` landing route: if `surface` is `public`, instructions MUST explicitly require `MarketingHero` + `PublicShell` composition and a bold premium AI-native 2026 storefront feel for THIS brand.
- For `/` home and every role `defaultPath` landing route: if `surface` is `ops`, instructions MUST explicitly require `OpsShell` + `PageHeader` + `StatCard` + (`ChartCard` and/or `DataTable`) composition in a polished calm SaaS ops style.
- Focused flow pages (checkout, consult wizard, onboarding, payment, confirmation, single-purpose forms) may be exceptions to the full shell requirement, but must still feel premium, polished, and built from the existing ui kit.